James wrote:
>
> According to NetHackWiki
> (http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Anti-magic_trap#.5E_Falling_rock_trap),
> a falling rock trap can be disarmed by triggering it repeatedly
> until it runs out of rocks; nothing else is mentionned.  From
> memory, I have the impression that anytime there is a falling
> rock trap, there is a boulder nearby (about 2 squares away), and
> moving this boulder seems to disarm the trap as well.  Is this
> right, or was this just coincidence a couple of times which gave
> me this impression?

Rolling boulder trap and falling rock trap are two distinct types.  A
rolling boulder trap gives up if it fails to roll its boulder.  A
falling rock trap is like an arrow trap - Each trigger does a roll to
see if it runs out.


